587f-bd0a-7296d778059b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115095 #edb/ref 1074 "The function $y = f\\left(\\dfrac{1}{4}x\\right)$ represents a stretch of the function $y = f(x)$ by a factor of $4$ parallel to the $x$-axis. This has the effect of multiplying the $x$-coordinates of all points on $y=f(x)$ by $4.$\n\nTherefore, the point $(6,7)$ on $f(x)$ is mapped to the point $\\left(4\\cdot 6 , 7\\right) = (24,7),$ and this point must lie on the graph of $y = f\\left(\\dfrac{1}{4}x\\right).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115264 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115517 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115264 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115520 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115264 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186530509 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115264 #edb/ref 1039 "Plotting the Graph of a Horizontally Stretched Function" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115264 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186115093 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115264 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "bd783d1a-745d-5cd7-a5c3-9a109b6d1350" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115265 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048838 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115265 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115522 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115265 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115523 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115265 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186530501 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115265 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186530516 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115265 #edb/ref 1039 "Plotting the Graph of a Horizontally Compressed Function" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115265 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186115094 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115265 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "d199ed2c-8188-5d80-9bb6-7b69ae684747" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115266 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115629 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115266 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115953 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115266 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186530435 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115266 #edb/ref